{
  "$comment": "Worked queue vectors (draft-backend §5.6/§5.7, package B-RPC). Data, not code: the queue algorithm lives only in SQL (M5). queue-vectors.schema.test.ts validates the shape (no DB); the maintainer-only draft RPC parity suite (private companion overlay, DRAFT_RPC_LIVE_DB=1) replays every case against a LOCAL supabase stack. Times are seconds from T0 = draft start (initial) or publish (redraft). Queue labels: '<sort_key> <alias>' plus '(m)' for a make-up slot; the current slot comes first. Default seats Brock=S(1) Serena=B(2) Dawn=K(3) Misty=N(4), roster 3, live 300/150 s, slow ladder 12h/6h/3h/1.5h; a pick step takes the cheapest legal line of that suite's list fixture (its default budget unless setup.budgets says otherwise). Additive fields beyond §5.7: setup.ladder, steps 'assign'/'forfeit', expect.durations (label -> seconds), expect.done (aliases), expect.paused (pool pause_reason).",
  "vectors": [
    {
